Administer a Nexo server through its Admin API: server information and usage,
users, groups, policies, access keys, configuration, service control, the export and
import of the state of a deployment, the lock diagnostics, the KMS of the
server-side encryption, the notification targets, the live trace of the requests
and the live logs, the audit log, the metrics and their Prometheus configuration,
the runtime profiles, the speed tests, the metadata log of the drives and the DNS
providers of the ACME DNS-01 challenge.

The Admin API is served by the console listener of the server: see --admin-url
of "nexoctl alias set". Every subcommand takes the alias as its first argument.

Usage:
  nexoctl admin [flags]
  nexoctl admin [command]

Available Commands:
  accesskey    Manage the access keys (service accounts) of the users
  audit        Search the audit log of the server
  cluster      Export and import the state of a deployment (IAM, policies, configuration, bucket settings)
  config       Read and change the dynamic configuration of the server
  dns-provider Manage the DNS providers of the ACME DNS-01 challenge
  group        Manage the IAM groups and their members
  heal         Heal the drives of the server (erasure-coded deployments)
  info         Show the server: version, mode, nodes and drives
  kms          Show the KMS of the server-side encryption and manage its keys
  lock         List and release the namespace locks of a cluster
  logs         Show the logs of the server, live
  metadata-log Inspect and compact the metadata log of the drives
  metrics      Query the recent metrics kept by the server
  notify       Inspect and test the notification targets
  policy       Manage the IAM policies (AWS policy language)
  profile      Collect a runtime profile (pprof) of the server
  prometheus   Integrate the metrics of the server with Prometheus
  service      Restart or stop the server
  speedtest    Measure the drives, the object layer or the network between the nodes
  trace        Show the requests served by the server, live
  usage        Show the data usage of the server and of each bucket
  user         Manage the IAM users

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for admin

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin [command] --help" for more information about a command.
